The defect is the silence rather than the missing auth. Serve has never offered built-in auth, which is a defensible position. But `engine_kwargs` is `Dict[str, Any]` described as carrying every knob vLLM provides, so `api_key` validates clean, and `runtime_env` carries `VLLM_API_KEY` to the replicas. No error, no warning, open endpoint.

Whatever is decided about terminating auth, accepting the key and failing open without a word is hard to defend. Rejecting it at config validation is the floor. @khushali9 has a plan that fits the existing design, `get_user_id` already documents that it expects an auth middleware to set `request.state.user_id`, and has asked to be pointed at a maintainer.

